    "title": "Residents Push For Laxer Watering Regs - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Bray ,\n1 days ago ORLEANS – Cape Cod’s drought status has dropped from a Level 2 to a Level 1. But does that mean that existing watering restrictions can be softened?. That’s the hope of residents who appeared before the town’s board of water and sewer commissioners May 20. They requested that some leeway be given to allow for outdoor watering one day a week. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
